                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Wish I could give this a neutral vote. I like what this game tries to do with its storytelling and gameplay, but I think this is a bit too barebones and empty to be worth paying full price for, especially for how short it is. It also lacks quite a bit of polish, especially enemy AI: the way they attack and move is pretty interesting, but also makes a fair amount of them very easy to manipulate into never attacking, and often they get stuck on terrain.\n\nThere are design elements that don't feel fleshed out. You've got very little reason to attack most monsters, some weapons and spells are vastly superior to others, the bosses could've been a little more interesting for how few of them there are. I feel like this game has the right bones to be much grander and more epic than it currently is, if only it had the dev team, the resources and the time to pull it off.\n\nI did enjoy my time with it still! If you're at all curious, you may want to grab this on sale. It might click with you! Sadly for most people I would not recommend it.",
